1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:08,887
The princess Sāvitrī shone so brightly that no prince dared ask for her hand.

2
00:00:08,887 --> 00:00:12,235
So she went forth to choose for herself —

3
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:18,522
and in a forest hermitage she chose Satyavān, son of a blind and exiled king.

4
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:32,642
But the sage Nārada brought her father news no father wants to hear: the boy was flawless in every virtue that mattered —

5
00:00:32,642 --> 00:00:39,249
and in one year, he would die. Sāvitrī answered only, "The heart is given once.

6
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:40,838
I have given mine."

7
00:00:45,038 --> 00:00:52,629
She folded away her silks, put on rough bark-cloth, and took up the hermitage's small daily work —

8
00:00:52,629 --> 00:00:55,650
telling no one, only counting the days.

9
00:00:55,650 --> 00:01:01,614
For the last three nights she stood fasting, still as a lamp in windless air.

10
00:01:06,014 --> 00:01:11,031
On the appointed morning she followed him into the forest.

11
00:01:11,031 --> 00:01:18,037
At noon, the axe slipped from Satyavān's hand. "My head," he said, "is splitting.

12
00:01:18,037 --> 00:01:21,756
" And he laid it in her lap, and was still.

13
00:01:27,156 --> 00:01:35,015
Then Sāvitrī saw him: a figure dark as a rain-cloud, robed in red, a noose coiled in his hand.

14
00:01:35,015 --> 00:01:40,784
It was Yama, King of the Dead, come in person for so virtuous a soul.

15
00:01:40,784 --> 00:01:47,389
He drew out a spark no bigger than a thumb, and turned south. And she followed.

16
00:01:52,789 --> 00:01:58,914
"Walk with the wise but seven steps," she said, "and you are friends.

17
00:01:58,914 --> 00:02:05,926
" Pleased, Yama offered her boon after boon — anything but the life he carried.

18
00:02:05,926 --> 00:02:09,920
Sight for the blind king. A kingdom restored.

19
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:15,246
And then, quietly: "a hundred sons, born of me and Satyavān.

20
00:02:15,246 --> 00:02:18,441
" The Lord of Death stopped walking.

21
00:02:22,841 --> 00:02:27,788
For her word could not come true unless his life was returned.

22
00:02:27,788 --> 00:02:32,416
Caught by his own boon, Yama smiled, and loosed the noose.

23
00:02:32,416 --> 00:02:39,039
Satyavān woke as if from sleep, and his father opened his eyes on a world made new.

24
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:44,784
Sāvitrī walked her husband home at dusk, having out-argued Death itself.
